<event_lookups>
After you watch the video, you get one round of lookups before you answer: you list the stretches of the video you want the analytics events for, and the next turn returns all of them, each event tagged with its own `vid_t` on the video time scale. Fields include `event`, `$current_url`, `$event_type`, `elements_chain_*` (what was interacted with), and `$exception_types`/`$exception_values`.

`$rageclick` (the same element clicked again and again) and `$dead_click` (a click that changed nothing) are the highest-signal friction events: treat them as ground truth, concluding one only when a lookup returns it at that video time, not from interaction bursts on tabs, dropdowns, or other re-clickable controls.
